  soaringWeather: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 50d9fcea1d5790f46a7b4432eb0d5b13, type: 2}
  displayName: Circuit and landing
  briefing: "SGS 2-33A / PA-18 development reference, 950 lb dual glider loading.
    These are simulator modules, not a Mile High syllabus or training credit. Physical
    inspection and crew communication are explained, not scored as performed. Reference08
    inside circuit: downwind south of the powered900m-north track and Jay Road; base
    east of the outer -1900m approach. Plan unpowered descent toward the paved centerline30m
    south of the local reference. Final42\u201358kt is a software practice window.
    No engine escape or automatic relocation."
  briefingNarration: {fileID: 0}
  learningGoal: Circuit and landing using measured controls, native state and sustained
    conditions.
  reflection: Which outside cue and instrument supported your decision? What margin
    would you require before an instructor-reviewed real flight?
  start:
    latitudeDegrees: 40.044318495468026
    longitudeDegrees: -105.2202305683336
    altitudeMslMeters: 1920.2824
    terrainElevationMslMeters: 1588.262401449585
    calibratedAirspeedKnots: 50
    headingDegrees: 270
    pitchDegrees: 0
    bankDegrees: 0
    flightPathAngleDegrees: -2.862400417
    engineRunning: 0
  initialThrottle: 0
  initialTrim: 0.10626088
  initialFlaps: 0
  allowDemonstration: 0
  airportExercise: 1
  goAroundStage: -1
  stages:
  - title: Inside downwind
    instruction: Fly west on the inside north-side downwind. Reach the western half
      above180m field height.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    successFeedback: Inside downwind was observed within the reference practice window.
    retryAdvice: Plan energy early and stay inside the powered pattern.
    task: 114
    reference: 0
    attitudeOnly: 0
    heading: 90
    altitudeFeet: 7000
    speedKnots: 50
    dwellSeconds: 3
    timeoutSeconds: 300
    targetEnu: {x: -500, y: 575}
    captureMeters: 200
  - title: Base turn
    instruction: Turn south on base between700m and1800m west of the reference.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    successFeedback: Base turn was observed within the reference practice window.
    retryAdvice: Use airbrakes as needed; preserve a safe speed and landing margin.
    task: 115
    reference: 0
    attitudeOnly: 0
    heading: 90
    altitudeFeet: 7000
    speedKnots: 50
    dwellSeconds: 2
    timeoutSeconds: 300
    targetEnu: {x: -1250, y: 350}
    captureMeters: 200
  - title: Stable final
    instruction: "Align east toward the paved centerline at42\u201358kt with controlled
      descent."
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    successFeedback: Stable final was observed within the reference practice window.
    retryAdvice: Use pitch and airbrakes; there is no powered go-around.
    task: 116
    reference: 0
    attitudeOnly: 0
    heading: 90
    altitudeFeet: 7000
    speedKnots: 50
    dwellSeconds: 3
    timeoutSeconds: 300
    targetEnu: {x: -1000, y: -30}
    captureMeters: 200
  - title: Touchdown
    instruction: Round out and land on the reference paved strip with wings level.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    successFeedback: Touchdown was observed within the reference practice window.
    retryAdvice: Reduce sink and bank before contact; a hard or off-runway touchdown
      needs another attempt.
    task: 117
    reference: 0
    attitudeOnly: 0
    heading: 90
    altitudeFeet: 7000
    speedKnots: 50
    dwellSeconds: 1
    timeoutSeconds: 300
    targetEnu: {x: -400, y: -30}
    captureMeters: 200
  - title: Rollout and stop
    instruction: Apply the last part of the combined lever for wheel braking and
      stop on the strip.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    successFeedback: Rollout and stop was observed within the reference practice
      window.
    retryAdvice: Stay aligned and hold the wheel brake; crew movement is a later
      explicit action.
